{"name":"Buccaneer","hex":"#6e5150","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"buccaneer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of seamen who cruised on their own account on the Spanish Main and in the Pacific in the 17th century, who were similar to pirates but did not prey on ships of their own nation.","A pirate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To engage in piracy against any but one's own nation's ships."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buccaneer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buccaneer","blocks":[{"text":"Buccaneers were privateers and pirates operating in the Caribbean Sea during the 17th and 18th centuries. First established as early as 1625 on northwestern side of Hispaniola after the devastations of Osorio, their heyday was from the Restoration in 1660 until about 1688, during a time when governments in the Caribbean area were not strong enough to suppress them. Martinique was a home port for French buccaneers as well as pirates like Captain Crapeau."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Pyle_pirate_handsome.jpg/330px-Pyle_pirate_handsome.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buccaneer"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Pyle_pirates_approaching_ship.jpg/500px-Pyle_pirates_approaching_ship.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Pyle_pirates_approaching_ship.jpg/1280px-Pyle_pirates_approaching_ship.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Pyle_pirates_approaching_ship.jpg/500px-Pyle_pirates_approaching_ship.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Howard Pyle – Buccaneers attacking a much larger Spanish galleon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APyle_pirates_approaching_ship.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Pyle_pirates_city.jpg/500px-Pyle_pirates_city.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Pyle_pirates_city.jpg/1280px-Pyle_pirates_city.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Pyle_pirates_city.jpg/500px-Pyle_pirates_city.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Howard Pyle – Buccaneers extorting tribute from the citizens of a captured city.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APyle_pirates_city.jpg"}],"sounds":{"buccaneer":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/91/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-buccaneer.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/91/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-buccaneer.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-buccaneer.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/91/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-buccaneer.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-buccaneer.wav.ogg"}]}}}